{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And in the commandment of loading He added to admonish concerning it with a negative commandment, for in the Torah it says (Exodus 23:5) <b>עָזֹב תַּעֲזֹב עִמּוֹ</b> (you shall surely release it with him), a positive commandment. And He further added <b>נוֹפְלִים בַּדֶּרֶךְ</b> (fallen on the road), for there He said <b>רוֹבֵץ תַּחַת מַשָּׂאוֹ</b> (crouching under its burden), and there He mentioned only the donkey, whose way is to carry a heavy load and to crouch beneath it. And here He said <b>אָחִיךָ</b> (your brother) and there <b>אוֹיִבְךָ</b> (your enemy) and <b>שׂוֹנַאֲךָ</b> (him who hates you), to say that you shall do the same with him, and remember the brotherhood and forget the hatred:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:53.545868686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}